et is FIXED to FILE struct addresses (not attacker-controlled). PoC outputs '=== PRIM-002: VERIFIED ==='.\"},\"confidence\":\"HIGH\",\"notes\":\"RELATIVE_WRITE (not ARB_WRITE): write target is fixed to FILE structure addresses determined by the negative index (-4=stderr, -6=stdin, -8=stdout). Attacker controls write content and size is unlimited. Two-step write to ARB_WRITE assessed but NOT feasible: msg[] array entries are set by create_cookie (calloc result), eat_cookie (pointer swap), and init (strdup result) - none allow attacker to place an arbitrary address value into a msg[] slot. The write is DIRECT (no intermediate heap/tcache operations). Combined with BUG-003 (integer underflow in size) for unlimited write size.\"},{\"primitive_id\":\"PRIM-003\",\"type\":\"NULL_POINTER_DEREF\",\"status\":\"VERIFIED\",\"kind\":\"DIRECT\",\"source\":{\"bug_id\":\"BUG-001\",\"root_cause\":\"Signedness mismatch in index check allows negative indices. Some negative indices hit BSS slots containing NULL (0x0000000000000000), which are then dereferenced as buffer pointers by read().\",\"description\":\"edit_cookie with negative index hitting a NULL-valued BSS slot (e.g., index -3 at 0x4048=completed.0=0) causes read(0, NULL, 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF), resulting in SIGSEGV due to NULL pointer dereference.\"},\"chain\":[\"BUG-001: OOB signedness mismatch in index check\",\"edit_cookie: negative index -3 passes signed jl check\",\"msg[-3] reads 0x0000000000000000 (NULL, completed.0 at 0x4048)\",\"read(0, NULL, 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF) dereferences NULL\",\"SIGSEGV - NULL pointer dereference\"],\"controlled_element\":{\"what\":\"Index value (negative) selecting which BSS slot to dereference; NULL-valued slots cause crash\",\"how\":\"Attacker sends negative cookie_index via scanf(\\\"%lld\\\") in edit_cookie (menu option 3)\",\"reach_sensitive_operation\":true},\"preconditions\":[{\"id\":\"PC-01\",\"description\":\"cookie_index must be negative to pass signed jl check\",\"necessity\":\"Required